# Audio, features, and model weights are large and often license-encumbered.
# Nothing under these is committed - see MODELS_AND_DATASETS.md for why.
# The folder patterns are anchored to the repo root. Unanchored, `audio/` also matched the
# src/workbench/audio/ package, which silently kept its source out of git (FIX-1).
/audio/
/models/
*.wav
*.flac
*.mp3
*.aiff
*.ogg
*.onnx
*.npy
*.npz
*.h5
*.zarr/

# Working material
experiments/**/out/
scratch/

# Per-machine agent tooling artifacts: instruction files, verbosity config, caches and indexes
# that a tool regenerates in the working tree rather than a human authoring them.
# Added 2026-09-21 for the AI Token Optimizer extension, which wrote all of these. That extension
# was removed fleet-wide on 2026-11-17 and nothing writes them today; the lines stay as insurance,
# because the cost of keeping them is nothing and the cost of committing one is a public repo
# carrying another machine's state. If a file below reappears, something is installed again.
CLAUDE.md
.codex/
.cavemanrc
.aicache/
.codegraph/

# Editor tooling writes MCP servers with absolute local paths into .vscode/settings.json, and this
# repo is public. Shared editor settings belong in the multi-root .code-workspace, which is
# authored and reviewable. LabsHQ ruled on this 2026-09-21: ignore it, do not track a redacted copy.
.vscode/settings.json
